// THE EMBASSY COUNCIL: the UAE ambassador's country team, in the structure of an embassy and of a foreign ministry's country desks, with a Chief of Staff (the Deputy Chief of Mission's role) who briefs the ambassador, keeps the updates and answers questions from what the team has found.
// Thirteen desks, each a PhD-level specialist with decades of practice (archetypes: no real person is represented). Two sittings, each under the US$1.00 ceiling: the INTELLIGENCE sitting (what is the situation, who matters, where the money and the partners are) and the PLAN sitting (what the mission does about it in 100 days, one year and three years, with owners, KPIs, due diligence and gates). Directives and questions go to the desks whose field they touch.
// Benchmarks the structure follows, as published: the US country-team model and Integrated Country Strategy (mission goals, objectives, lines of effort, measures), ambassador briefing books (bottom line first, the leaders and the power map, bilateral issues, calendar, what not to do, who to see), foreign-ministry country-strategy practice, and the analytic standards of ICD 203 as a method. Not a claim about any agency, and no signals or classified access.
